  "note": "[H] assembles (quan) for t >= 2000 into 0.10848 t^{3/2} term by term (main term 0.10181 t^{3/2}); Lean does the analogous assembly for its own terms, for L = t/3 >= 70 (t >= 210), with total 1.413 L^{3/2} = 0.2719 t^{3/2}; none of the displayed constants 0.00012, 0.00145, 0.000048, 0.00462 occur. Lean writes T = x^{1/3}, L = log T, so x^{2/3} = T^2 and log x = 3L; Lean's second choice differs from [H]'s (U = floor(1225T), V = floor(T/3), re-approximation parameter Q0 = T^2/349 instead of Q = x/U; see NOTES.md).",
